{"id": "EUVD-2026-59438", "enisaUuid": "2e917f43-ce06-31cb-aef0-0a2c2d41fb75", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: topology: Check PCM and DAI name strings before use\n\nTopology objects store several PCM and DAI names in fixed-size UAPI\narrays. Other topology parser paths validate these fields with bounded\nstrnlen() checks before using them as C strings, but the PCM and DAI\npaths still pass some fixed-size arrays directly to strlen(),\ndevm_kstrdup(), DAI lookup, and diagnostic prints.\n\nA malformed topology blob with a non-NUL-terminated PCM, DAI, or stream\ncapability name can therefore make the parser read past the end of the\nfixed-size field.\n\nReject unterminated PCM and DAI name fields before consuming them as C\nstrings.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:57:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:55:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c405b07246bf179e9457de57501c3470175b165e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/473f7d25d93e80db526a9d05887f0071abdc6d9b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5c2537cf24d673956b4e58029001667f89586fa2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ba37b62ed0a443b8e23f53a7477e7f2537fd34c7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7e44d1986d6671342c19b82192189ca5db5dab7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wrjf-2g4j-cfrg", "CVE-2026-74291"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "112f1dfb-c206-345d-a23c-c3916168ca69", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "11b8d417-a769-3c4a-938f-6f43080761cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "36082640-de46-3b37-bbe8-3d6433848b8a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64527e8a352968bda529f01df1c9dd5fe581ff04 <5c2537cf24d673956b4e58029001667f89586fa2"}, {"id": "573b7012-361f-3521-ad38-0bd59b3dd800", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64527e8a352968bda529f01df1c9dd5fe581ff04 <473f7d25d93e80db526a9d05887f0071abdc6d9b"}, {"id": "5fd13a52-d212-37b0-b0c5-2fda53129cc9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "80759fc1-6cec-3685-814e-d5754f417519", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64527e8a352968bda529f01df1c9dd5fe581ff04 <c405b07246bf179e9457de57501c3470175b165e"}, {"id": "a6e3cd86-853b-3db2-8327-6208ff564a44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64527e8a352968bda529f01df1c9dd5fe581ff04 <ba37b62ed0a443b8e23f53a7477e7f2537fd34c7"}, {"id": "cbbcc9d9-b4e3-386f-b4b6-c8863b01e4cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.6"}, {"id": "e3c0419f-f01c-375b-b527-9a6354fba241", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e992d9c0-3aa5-3e18-aab9-2f71cc102a18", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64527e8a352968bda529f01df1c9dd5fe581ff04 <b7e44d1986d6671342c19b82192189ca5db5dab7"}, {"id": "f190f968-a97d-3290-a2b3-06693682e66e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "fafc4c82-0be9-30df-b790-0e4045b32e59", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bab9e945-eaa1-3f83-9331-6d45f3fac316", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}